Canberra is often overlooked by international students — and that's a mistake. Australia's capital has the country's highest graduate employment rate, highest median income, and an increasingly vibrant food and arts scene. For students at ANU or UC, it's a compact, safe city that punches above its weight.

## Canberra Housing Market 2026

Canberra has Australia's highest median rent — but that's driven by family homes in premium suburbs. Student accommodation is more affordable than the headline numbers suggest. Shared housing near ANU runs AUD 220–380/week for a room, with studios starting around AUD 380/week.

## ANU — Acton & the Inner North

The Australian National University sits in Acton, wedged between the CBD and Lake Burley Griffin.

### Acton & Civic (CBD)
Immediate walking distance to campus. Mostly apartment buildings. Studios AUD 400–550/week, shared rooms AUD 250–380/week.

### Braddon
The coolest neighborhood in Canberra. Lonsdale Street's restaurants, bars, and boutiques are a 10-minute walk from ANU. Rooms AUD 240–360/week.

### Turner & O'Connor
Quiet, leafy suburbs bordering the ANU campus. Popular with postgrad students. Rooms AUD 220–340/week.

### Dickson
Canberra's Chinatown. Great Asian supermarkets and restaurants on Woolley Street. 15-minute bus to ANU. Rooms AUD 200–300/week.

## University of Canberra — Belconnen

UC is in Bruce, part of the Belconnen district north of the city centre.

### Bruce & Belconnen Town Centre
The Belconnen Town Centre has a Westfield, fresh food markets, and the bus interchange. Rooms AUD 180–280/week.

### Macquarie & Aranda
Suburbs between UC and the city. Quiet, established neighborhoods popular with families and students. Rooms AUD 180–280/week.

## On-Campus Housing

Both ANU and UC have extensive on-campus accommodation options:

### ANU Halls & Lodges
- **Catered halls** (Burgmann, John XXIII, Ursula Hall): AUD 380–480/week including meals
- **Self-catered lodges** (Davey, Kinloch, Warrumbul): AUD 280–380/week
- Apply through ANU Accommodation Services — deadline usually October for February start

### UC Campus West & Cooper Lodge
- Self-catered apartments from AUD 220/week (shared) to AUD 360/week (studio)
- All within the Belconnen campus grounds


## FAQ

### Is Canberra too quiet for students?
Canberra has transformed in the last five years. Braddon, NewActon, and the Kingston Foreshore now have a genuine nightlife and dining scene. It's smaller than Sydney or Melbourne, but the concentration of young professionals and students means there's always something happening.

### What's the weather like?
Four distinct seasons. Winters are cold (often below 0°C overnight) but dry and sunny. Summers are warm (25–35°C). You'll need heating and good winter clothing — something many international students from warm climates underestimate.

### Is OSHC required for ANU?
Yes — [mandatory OSHC for all international students in Australia](https://agents.flywire.com/services/Unilink/oshc-au?referrer=0df195ef-7f4d-4faf-82e2-1878faa84597).

